{"name":"Left on Red","hex":"#ff0303","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"left","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Designating the side of the body toward the west when one is facing north; the side of the body on which the heart is located in most humans; the opposite of right. This arrow points to the reader's left: ←","Anticlockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On the left side.","Towards the left side."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/left"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turn on red","blocks":[{"text":"Turn on red is a principle of law permitting vehicles at a traffic light showing a red signal to turn into the direction of traffic nearer to them when the way is clear, without having to wait for a green signal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/330px-Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turn_on_red"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/500px-Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/1280px-Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/500px-Right-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A BMW hatchback makes a right turn on red in New York State.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARight-turn-on-red-nys.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/500px-Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/1280px-Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg/500px-Left-turn-on-red-nys.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traffic turns left on red between one-way roads in Poughkeepsie, NY","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeft-turn-on-red-nys.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Right_turn_on_red_%28cropped%29.jpg/120px-Right_turn_on_